WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.680
Know your customer, set up your kit, and plan with numbers.

2
00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:10.510
This is the video for module one of Digital Marketing Fundamentals: customers, channels and a plan.

3
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:19.640
Marketing is everything you do to help the right people discover you, trust you, buy and come back. The funnel maps that journey.

4
00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:25.280
Awareness is when someone sees your post or your shop on Google Maps for the first time.

5
00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:32.410
Consideration is when she looks at your catalog, reads reviews and asks the price on WhatsApp.

6
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.430
Conversion is when she pays.

7
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.740
Loyalty is when she buys again and tells her friends.

8
00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:50.750
When sales are low, the funnel shows where. Many views but no messages? Perhaps your price is hidden. Many messages but few payments? Perhaps you reply too slowly.

9
00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:01.030
Amaka sells small chops in Port Harcourt, and compares two ways to promote one weekend. These prices are illustrative and approximate.

10
00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:09.740
Option A. Print 500 flyers for about 15,000 naira, and pay a helper about 5,000 to share them.

11
00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:18.970
That is about 20,000 naira to reach 500 people. Per 1,000 people, that is about 40,000 naira.

12
00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:25.660
The flyers brought 3 orders. She knew, because she asked each caller where they heard of her.

13
00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:37.680
Option B. An ad for about 10,000 naira reached 8,000 people, about 1,250 naira per 1,000 people, and brought 5 orders.

14
00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:48.550
So she keeps a few flyers for her street, and moves most of her budget to the ad. But remember, reach is not sales. Follow the funnel down to orders before you decide.

15
00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:57.760
My product is for everybody is a common mistake. Ads charge for every view, and a message for everyone speaks to no one.

16
00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:05.130
Bisi cooks meal packs in Abuja. She looked at her last 30 orders and talked to six regular customers.

17
00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:12.310
22 of the 30 orders came from women, most working in offices in Wuse and Garki.

18
00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:18.640
Their biggest problem was coming home too tired to cook, and worrying about fast food.

19
00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:25.180
Most ordered on Sunday evening after seeing her WhatsApp Status, and paid by transfer.

20
00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:40.550
Her value proposition: home-style Nigerian meals for busy Abuja families, cooked fresh on Sunday and delivered to your door. Base yours on real orders and real conversations, not imagination.

21
00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:49.860
Many businesses pay for ads before their own channels are ready, so visitors arrive at an empty page and leave. Build first.

22
00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:59.320
Funke in Ogbomosho moved her number to WhatsApp Business, filled every profile field, and added 12 outfits to her catalog with prices.

23
00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:05.540
She created a free Google Business Profile, so people searching near me can find her.

24
00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:11.150
Choose one platform where your customers already spend time, and do it well.

25
00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:17.090
She put her wa dot me link in her Instagram bio, so one tap opens a chat.

26
00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:24.060
Keep your name, address and phone number identical everywhere, so customers and Google trust you.

27
00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:30.000
And protect your accounts. Anyone who gets your verification code can take over your account.

28
00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:41.270
I want more customers is a wish, not a goal. Bisi's goal is 40 meal-pack orders in March. Followers and likes do not pay rent, so aim at orders.

29
00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:52.420
Her notebook shows 20 of every 100 people who chat with her order. That is a 20% conversion rate. So 40 orders need 200 chats.

30
00:03:53.670 --> 00:04:01.410
And 2 of every 100 people who see her posts send a message. So 200 chats need 10,000 people reached.

31
00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:12.670
If she replies faster and lifts her rate to 25%, she needs only 160 chats. Fixing the bottom of the funnel is often cheaper than buying reach.

32
00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:24.260
To remember. Use owned, earned and paid media together. Pick one specific customer. Build your starter kit before ads. Set goals on orders, not likes.

33
00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:28.640
And in your budget, spend only what you can afford to lose while you learn.

34
00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:40.200
Now practise. Map your channels on the funnel, interview three customers, complete your starter kit, and write your one-page 90-day plan with the funnel sum shown.

35
00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:42.490
Continue with the lessons below.
